message: "If you use this reference, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "The Cybersecurity Command Reference — Authorized Operator Edition"
abstract: >
  A methodology-verified reference of Linux commands used by
  security operators. Each entry documents function, canonical
  syntax, curated options, worked examples with expected output,
  interpretation guidance, operational cautions, MITRE ATT&CK
  mapping, and detection signals. Verified against Ubuntu 22.04,
  Rocky Linux 9.3, and Arch Linux 2024.01.
